# Gantry — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Gantry carries a debugging and automation surface, `window.__gantry`, so a site
can be posed and read from code without moving a real pointer or waiting on
real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__gantry` as soon as the game
has initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it,
so it is present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a reading or a pose. A pose sets one thing and leaves the
rest of the game as it stands, so a caller that wants several things arranged
makes several calls, in the order it wants them, and nothing it does not ask
for happens. A pose arranges the yard through the same systems play uses: a
posed edit passes the placement rules a click passes, a posed tape step passes
the rules the tape editor applies, and a run started through the surface is the
run the `run` action starts. A pose establishes a precondition and never an
outcome; what happens next comes from advancing the real simulation.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls
it.
